<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|article>

<\body>
  <section|A nested derivation>

  Click in this paragraph and type. The caret belongs to the document itself.

  <\theorem>
    For every real <math|x>, the expression <math|<frac|x<rsup|2>+1|2>> is positive.
  </theorem>

  <\equation*>
    A=<matrix|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|1>|<cell|<frac|x<rsup|2>|2>>>|<row|<cell|0>|<cell|1>>>>>
  </equation*>

  In the matrix, move the caret into the numerator to see its enclosing
  tags. To expose the tags, choose <strong|Document>, then
  <strong|Source>, then <strong|Edit source tree>.
</body>
